bject's size, or of a static struct's)."] [195 2 "// the function slots: a C type's own (its spec's or PyType_Ready's, inherited), else the generic natives"] [201 57 "// tp_doc: the spec's copy (queue 270b)"] [203 3 "// ht_name, ht_qualname (queue 270b: test_type_from_ephemeral_spec reads them)"] [206 3 "// ht_module (queue 521: _decimal's find_state_left_or_right reads it in place, pycore_typeobject.h's inline"] [207 3 "// _PyType_GetModuleState), the module PyType_FromModuleAndSpec named, kept for the process as the type is"] [252 1 "// classNew reports whether t's __new__ is a class statement's (the first dictionary of its MRO holding __new__ is a"] [253 1 "// pyi class's, not a built-in's or a C type's): its tp_new is then CPython's slot_tp_new (Objects/typeobject.c,"] [254 1 "// type_new's tp_new for a class whose namespace defines __new__, which its subclasses inherit), the class's __new__"] [255 1 "// called, not its built-in base's (_pickle's load_newobj calls cls->tp_new: a list or tuple subclass's __new__,"] [256 1 "// test_descr's test_reduce_copying, a NamedTuple's, test_enum's tuple subclasses)."] [269 1 "// storeSlot writes the function fn into the slot id of the type object at a (its sub-struct's field when the type"] [270 1 "// has that sub-struct)."] [283 1 "// loadSlot reads the slot id of the type object at a (0: none, or no sub-struct)."] [296 1 "// ---- mirrors ----"] [298 1 "// mirror is the CPython layout of a tuple, list, bytes, float, int or str in the world's memory, a handle's."] [300 17 "// 't' tuple, 'l' list, 'b' bytes, 'f' float, 'i' int, 'u' str"] [301 17 "// the pyi object (a subclass's instance too: its built-in part is mirrored)"] [302 17 "// a tuple's or list's slots as last synchronized"] [303 17 "// a bytes' contents as last synchronized"] [304 17 "// the synchronization epoch of the last copy from C"] [305 2 "// a str's (queue 270, capi_unicode.go): its kind, ASCII flag and characters' address; a str PyUnicode_New made"] [306 2