715 1 "// usedLists are the lists' mirrors natives used (touch) since the outermost entry into the world (World.Call, worldDepth"] [716 1 "// its nesting)."] [722 1 "// syncAllFromC copies every mirror's C state to its pyi value (when the world returns to Python)."] [730 1 "// nativeEnter and nativeLeave bracket a native's (or a closure's) run: what C wrote is copied to Go on the first use"] [731 1 "// of a mirrored object in it (fromHandle), and the mirrors it used are written back to C when it returns."] [752 1 "// touch marks a mirrored handle as used by the running native."] [764 1 "// ---- C types over a built-in base (268's DECISION (a), the user 2026-11-11) ----"] [766 1 "// born is a C type's instance over a built-in base (a type a spec or PyType_Ready made, deriving from list, tuple,"] [767 1 "// bytes or float): its memory is the world's, tp_basicsize bytes (and its items'), the built-in part a mirror of the"] [768 1 "// pyi value at its head, the extension's part C's after the base's size. The Go value is an instance of the type"] [769 1 "// keeping a built-in value, as a Python class deriving from the built-in keeps one; the record rides on it"] [770 1 "// (py.SetInstanceExt). Its memory lives as a C-born object's (queue 268): until Go collects the instance, then its"] [771 1 "// tp_dealloc runs on the world's next entry."] [779 1 "// bornKind is the mirrored layout of t's built-in base (0: none of them)."] [792 15 "// queue 270b: a spec over int (its mirror a PyLongObject's)"] [795 15 "// queue 270b: a spec over an exception (no mirror: C reads its fields through functions)"] [801 1 "// bornOf is o's record when o is a C type's instance over a built-in base (nil: none)."] [813 1 "// bornHandle is such an instance's handle: its memory's address, in the maps again (a count of 0: unowned until the"] [814 1 "// C entry ends; its mirror written from Go, which may have changed it meanwhile) when it had left them."] [831 1 "// bornNew is tp_alloc for a C type over a built-in base: the instance of sub with nitems items (a tuple's or bytes'),"] [832 1 "// a new reference."] [859 1 "// bornValue is the built-in value of a C type's instance over a built-in base its base's __new__ makes from the"] [860 1 "// arguments (queue 270b: a spec over int without tp_new, HeapCTypeWithBasesSlot(5)): the base's own value, or for an"] [861 1 "// exception the exception of sub itself."] [881 1 "// bornWith makes the instance of sub keeping the built-in value v (for an exception, v is the instance), its memory"] [882 1 "// the world's: tp_basicsize bytes (and nitems items') or the mirror's size, the built-in part mirrored."] [931 1 "// allocObj is tp_alloc's generic allocation of t (PyType_GenericAlloc): a C-born object, an instance over a built-in"] [932 1 "// base, or a type object's memory (type's own tp_alloc: a heap type C fills, then PyType_Ready's)."] [935 3 "// a type object (a C metaclass's too, queue 270b: its basicsize, the C tail after the PyHeapTypeObject)"] [956 3 "// a built-in type of pyi's whose zero value is an instance (queue 594: _io._BytesIOBuffer's tp_alloc in"] [957 3 "// test_pep3118_obsolete_write_locks): a new reference"] [969 1 "// rawTypes are the type objects C allocated through type's tp_alloc, not ready yet."] [972 1 "// bornDealloc is a built-in base's tp_dealloc on a C instance's memory (list_dealloc, tupledealloc ...): its items'"] [973 1 "// references given back as CPython's do, read from its memory, the list's array and the memory freed."] [995 1 "// ---- PyType_Ready for a type object of C's memory (a static PyTypeObject, or one C filled after type's tp_alloc) ----"] [997 1 "// typeReady is PyType_Ready (Objects/typeobject.c, type_ready) of the type object at a: a pyi type made from its"] [998 1 "// fields (NewExtType), its slots the C functions it names and those it inherits, its handle a; the fields"] [999 1 "// PyType_Ready fills written back (tp_base, tp_bases, tp_mro, tp_dict, the inherited slots,